[FEN "7k/3nr2p/2B3p1/1pp5/5p2/1PP5/5PP1/R5K1 w - - 0 37"]
[PlyCount "5"]

{Is there a way for White to win material here (except the pawn on b5 ) ?} 37. Ra8+ {It is important to drive the black king to the 7th rank.} ({Perhaps you thought the following move was better:} 37. Ra7 $2 Re1+ 38. Kh2 Ne5 {And Black unpins and achieves a much better position. This is why we should pay attention to the opponent's resources!}) 37... Kg7 38. Ra7 {Pin and win!} Re1+ 39. Kh2 {And the d7 -knight is now pinned to the black king, thanks to White's first move. What makes this position instructive is that White found the winning line by actively searching for the opponent's resources. White put himself in the opponent's shoes and 'refuted' the candidate move 37. Ra7 . Many upcoming players have difficulty in actively searching for the opponent's best options. In this course, we will train this very important ability to look for the opponent's moves that offer the most resistance against our moves.} *

