{This is a great example of goal-setting when calculating. Here Black has the queenside pawn majority and the goal should be the creation of a passed pawn. Black achieves the goal by using a short calculation.} 31... c3 {The queenside pawn majority rolls forward and Black creates a passed pawn by force.} 32. bxc3 b3 {The mission accomplished! As a result of this typical 'simulated pawn exchange', the b-pawn became a dangerous passer that will tie down the white queen.} 33. Qf5 b2 34. Qb1 Qa7+ 35. Kh1 Qa1 {Black wins. In this course, you will train the ability of goal-setting from the initial position: you will pay attention to the imbalances and make use of the imbalance that favors you, as the queenside pawn majority in this game. Chapter 3 will investigate further such positional mini-plans and strategic operations.} *

