[PlyCount "5"]

{Positional chess involves being aware of the weaknesses in the position. Weak pawns, weak squares, a weak king, etc. We form a plan in chess around the weaknesses and targets. Here, Black focuses on the pawn structure and makes a mini-plan to improve the position.} 22... c5 {The c7 -pawn was backward and weak. It could be targeted by Rac1 if given time. Thus, Black quickly removes a weakness while simultaneously hitting at the center and activating the rook on c8 . Slow play would favor White:} (22... Rd5 $2 23. Rac1 $1 {And White starts targeting the c7 -pawn as well as the weak c6 -square.} c5 24. e4 Rh5 25. g4 Rxh2 26. Rxc5 {And White obtains a slight advantage.}) 23. dxc5 Rxd1 24. Rxd1 Rxc5 {Strategic success for Black! Now there is no more a backward pawn on c7 and the rook got active as a result. Black has a slight pull in this ending, due to the more active rook. Notice how the black king is taking away all the entry squares from the white rook.} *

