{Can you spot a strong mini-plan for Black that aims to exploit a weakness?} 2... Qb4 {The art of exchanging pieces! As a result of this forcing move, the d4 -pawn will drop by force. It is usually a good policy to exchange pieces if the opponent has long-term, organic weaknesses in the position, as the d4 -pawn in this case. Note that slow play would only favor White:} (2... Qb5 $2 3. Nd3 {And the knight reached an ideal square where it not only stops ... Qb4 but also targets the weak square on e5 .}) 3. Qxb4 Rxb4 {And the d4 -pawn will be taken on the next move, with a much better ending for Black.} *

