[PlyCount "3"]

{Reti - Rubinstein, 1920. Can you find the winning mini-plan for Black?} 48... g5 {A very strong undermining move! Now the black king is gaining access to the e5 -square, and this spells trouble for White, who also has to deal with an outside passed pawn on a3 . White resigned here.} 49. fxg5 (49. e5+ fxe5 50. fxe5+ Kxe5) ({fxe5} 49. fxg5 {e4-+}) 49... fxg5 {As a result of the strong undermining plan, the black king became active and it will munch the pawns on e4 and g4 . However, the white king has to worry about the outside passed pawns on the queenside.} *

