[PlyCount "11"]

{One typical strategic operation is to use our pawns to destroy an enemy pawn chain. And ever since Nimzowitsch, we know that the base of the pawn chain should be attacked to reach this goal. Once the enemy pawn chain is destroyed, several weak pawns are created and our pieces gain activity as a result. In this game, White showed the idea in a very clear way.} 10. g6 {Destroying the pawn chain and activating the king. The destruction of the pawn chain can even take place in an endgame as in this example.} fxg6 (10... f6+ 11. Kxe6) 11. Kxe6 {As a result of the mini-plan, the white king has improved significantly, and the white rook gained scope along the 7th rank. Moreover, all three black pawns have now become weak. What else can you expect from a strategic mini-plan?} Kf8 12. Rf7+ Kg8 13. d7 g5 14. Rf5 g4 15. Ke7 {And White wins. In this course, you will be given an opportunity to destroy an enemy pawn chain and gain several strategic advantages.} *

