1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. h4 h6 5. g4 Bd7 6. c4 e6 7. c5 {White wants to gain space on the queenside and squeeze the black pieces even more. What is wrong with this move?} b6 {Putting a question mark to that pawn chain.} 8. b4 a5 {The correct followup to the first move! Now White's pawn chain on the queenside will be destroyed, and Black gains the advantage. Note that it is very important that White cannot keep the pawn chain intact with a2 - a3 here:} 9. a3 axb4 10. axb4 Rxa1 {Exploiting the pin along the a-file. A stock standard plan in several openings. 3-ply calculation helped Black achieve the strategic goal.} *

