[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "3. Positional Themes and Mini"]
[Black "Puzzle"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "r2qrbk1/1b1n1pp1/pp1p3p/2pPp3/4P1P1/2P1NN2/PPB1QP1P/1K1R3R w - - 0 17"]
[PlyCount "4"]

17. h4 {Opposite-side castling positions call for pawn storms and attacks. How should Black handle this upcoming pawn storm on the kingside?} g6 {Creating a padlock formation between the h- and g-pawns! This ensures Black in keeping the structure closed:} ({What happens if Black does not create the padlock formation?} 17... b5 $2 18. g5 $1 h5 19. g6 $1 {opens up the kingside and creates a winning attack.}) 18. g5 (18. h5 g5 $1 {Again, keeping the kingside closed and thus securing the black king.}) 18... h5 {As a result of the last move, Black could keep the kingside closed. White still has an edge due to the space advantage, but the black king won't be mated soon!} *

