{Here White has a lead in development and the black king wants to castle short next move. White forms a mini-plan to keep the enemy king in the center.} 11. exd6 {Opening up the e-file with tempo and preparing the next move.} (11. e6 {The attempt to bury the bishop on c8 would be wrong due to} fxe6 12. dxe6 d5 $1 {and Black will eventually capture the e6 -pawn. White's main goal was to keep the black king in the center from the initial position. but the e6-pawn is blocking the white pieces right now.}) 11... cxd6 12. Re1 {Preventing the black king from castling short. White thus intensifies the advantage in the lead in development. It is not clear how Black can untangle here. Mini-plan succeeded!} *

