{We need to have sound knowledge on the essential endgames. For example, we should know when a particular pawn endgame is winning. This knowledge will make it possible to engage in correct exchanges and transitions to a winning endgame. In this minor piece ending, Black has an extra pawn. Black executes a mini-plan to force a winning position:} 37... g5 {Forcing the knight to f3 and preparing the next move.} 38. Nf3 {The knight had no other square.} Bg4 {Forcing the exchange and transforming the game to a pawn ending, where Black's extra pawn will prove decisive.} 39. Ke3 Bxf3 40. Kxf3 f5 {And Black is winning easily in this pawn ending with a clear extra pawn. Black used a reversed engineering method here: he saw the pawn endgame as winning and found a way to get there with the minor piece trade. In this course, you will engage in 3-ply calculations to achieve a dream ending.} *

