{Can Black exploit the passed a-pawn here?} 2... Na4+ {A great square for the knight as it will support the passed pawn!} 3. Kc2 (3. Kb3 Nc5+ {forks the king and the rook.}) 3... a2 {And the pawn is unstoppable as the knight guards the b2 -square. Short and sweet!} *

