{Can you see a good idea for White here?} 30. g6 {Hitting the a5 -rook and preparing the next move.} (30. Bf7+ {does not work due to} Ke7 {and after} 31. Rxh7 Ne6+ 32. Bxe6+ Kxe6 {Black obtains equality.}) 30... Rxh5 (30... hxg6 31. Rxa5) 31. g7 {And White creates a passed pawn that cannot be stopped! Notice how an advanced passed pawn is bringing fascinating tactical opportunities. No wonder Nimzowitsch called passed pawns criminals!} *

