[PlyCount "4"]

21... Rxb6 {How should White recapture this rook?} 22. cxb6 {Creating a passer first.} Qb7 23. c5 {And making the b6 -pawn a protected passed pawn. After this short sequence, White obtains a completely winning positional advantage. Just observe how badly the black pieces stand here. The queens are the worst blockaders in chess, and the black bishop is buried too. Thanks to the protected passed pawn, White is also winning almost all pawn endings.} *

