{Please focus on the essence of this position and come up with a short sequence for White that is decisive.} 6. Bb5 {Removing the blockade! The d-pawn is free to roam now!} (6. Bxf7+ {would be a mistake:} Kxf7 7. Kxd7 Re2 8. Rd3 f2 {and Black's passer reaches the 2nd rank, gaining equality.}) 6... Bxb5 7. axb5 {And d6 - d7 is coming next with a decisive effect. Short and simple, right? The difficulty here was finding the very first move. That is why the hint given was to understand the essence of this position. White's main asset was the passed pawn on d6 , thus the correct candidate move was found after this initial orientation phase.} *

