{This example greatly shows the importance of generating several candidate moves while attacking while at the same time taking into account the opponent's resources. What should White do?} 11. Qg4 {A very forcing move!} (11. Qd4 $2 {This move would let Black defend:} Qg5 12. f4 Qh6 {And Black is in the game.}) 11... g6 {The g-pawn must move in order to avoid mate.} 12. Qd4 {With mate to follow soon. An elegant and simple calculation, which prevented ... Qg5 defensive resource. White generated two candidates from the initial position and chose the one that prevented the opponent's idea!} *

