[PlyCount "17"]

{Nikolic - Fischer, 1968. Can you guess the strong attacking plan executed by Fischer in this game?} 23... Bxf4 {Removing the defender and clearing the h-file for the upcoming plan.} 24. exf4 Kg7 {... Rh8 is coming now and Black's attack against the white king is already irresistible. Notice the choking effect of the fishbone pawn on f3 on the white king.} 25. f5 Rh8 {Fischer begins the assault on the h-file.} 26. Bh6+ {White gives up a piece but it won't save the white king.} (26. Rh4 Rxh4 27. gxh4 Qxf5) (26. Rxh8 Rxh8 {And ... Qxf5 will follow with a mating attack.}) 26... Rxh6 27. Rxh6 Kxh6 28. Qd2+ g5 29. bxc6 Qxf5 {Fischer does not lose time on the queenside.} 30. Nd1 Qh3 31. Ne3 Kg6 {White resigned as ... Rh8 is coming next with checkmate to follow.} *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "8. Attack"]
[Black "The Weakest Point Around the "]
[Result "*"]
