[PlyCount "3"]

{Najdorf - Gligoric, 1953. Here Black finds a strong resource that is based on several short lines.} 39... f3 {Opening up the king!} (39... Rh1 {would be a mistake due to} 40. Qg4 {and White is in the game as Qh4 is prevented and the g6 -bishop is pinned!}) 40. gxf3 {White has no safe capture of this pawn.} (40. Qxf3 Rf4) (40. Kxf3 Bh5+) (40. Qe3 fxg2 {opens the f-file with a winning position, e.g.} 41. Kxg2 Rh2+ {leads to a mating attack.}) 40... Rh2+ {Skewering the queen. Elegantly simple lines! As you see from this example, you often do not need to calculate very long lines and combinations to succeed in your attack. Short but accurate calculations will often do the job. In this course, we will train this ability and improve our attacking play by calculating short lines in a precise way.} *

