{Black's queen and knight duo coordinate beautifully towards the weakness on g2 . However, there is a check to deal with right now. Where should the black king go?} 35... Kg8 {A prudent retreat, anticipating White's next move, which is the only check in the position.} (35... Kf8 $4 {This terrible blunder would lose the game!} 36. Qh8+ Ke7 37. Bh4+) (35... Kh7 $2 {would allow a perpetual check} 36. Qxf7+ {.}) 36. Qd8+ Kh7 {There are no more checks left! Black thus avoids the perpetual check and White can not guard the g2 -point. Black wins.} 37. Kh3 Qxg2+ 38. Kh4 Qh1+ 39. Bh2 Qxh2# *

