{What is the principled way of defending this position?} 1... Rd2+ {Active defense!} (1... Ra8 {Not principled, as it allows the enemy rook to go behind the passed pawn.} 2. Ra3 Ra5 {This is the only move that draws. But it will be a long-suffering for Black to hold this position.}) 2. Kf3 Ra2 {Rooks belong behind the passed pawns! This is by far the best way to defend this position for Black.} 3. Rc4 Kf6 4. Kf4 Rf2+ 5. Ke3 Rg2 6. Kf3 Ra2 {Notice how annoying the black rook is in this position. Active defense saves the day with relative ease.} *

