{A typical Carlsbad structure on the board. White wants to execute the minority attack on the queenside with a4 and b4 - b5 . Black's knight on d7 has no business on that square. Can you find a good mini-plan for Black?} 1... b5 {The typical Carlsbad plan. Black is creating a good square for the knight and stopping White's queenside initiative.} 2. a4 Nb6 {Just before White goes a4 - a5 . The knight will become active and clog the queenside after ... Nc4 . The backward c6 -pawn can not be exploited after ... Nc4 as well. Later on, Black may switch to the kingside initiative with ... f5 - f4 , ... Bh6 , ... Nxe3 etc. See the relevant Positional theme.} *

