{Here White is down a pawn and Black has the bishop pair. White has a lead in development. The c1 -rook is attacked. How should White play here?} 19. Na5 {Acting fast, using the lead in development, and going for a counterattack, eyeing the weak c6 -square. Slow play would only help Black develop the bishop.} (19. Rc2 $2 Bf5) (19. Rce1 Be6) 19... Bxc1 (19... Be6 $1 {would be the best reaction for Black:} 20. Nc6+ Kc8 21. Nxb8 Bxc1 22. Nc6 Bg5 23. Nxd4 {White established the material balance, but Black is still a little better due to the bishop pair.}) 20. Nc6+ {And White is winning as the b8 -rook will be taken with check and White will have an extra piece after capturing the c1 -bishop. White only needs to see this short variation before going for the counterattacking move 19. Na5 . See the relevant Defensive Theme.} *

