{Ojjeh team - Nataf team, 2003. Here Black has the bishop pair and the d2 -knight is in trouble as moving it allows ... Be4 +. How can White save this position?} 26. Qa8 ({Active defense! Usually the best recipe.} 26. Nf3 $2 Qe2 {And ...Qf1+ will lead to disaster for White.}) (26. Qd8 $2 {would not work due to} Qxd2 27. Bxb4 Be4+ {wins the queen on d8 .}) 26... Qxd2 27. Bxb4 {And this short variation shows that White will regain the piece on f8 while also weakening the black king. The poor d2 -knight was not defended but White instead went for a counterattack.} h5 28. Qxf8+ Kh7 29. Qxf7 {Opposite-colored bishops favor the attacker, and here Black still has the initiative on the kingside, but the best Black can get is perpetual against the best defense :} Qd1 30. h4 Be4+ 31. f3 Qe2+ 32. Kg1 Qe1+ 33. Kg2 Qe2+ {See the relevant Defensive Theme.} *

