27. Rh2 {This was a game of mine in a classical game that I was proud of. Please take a moment and understand the essence here. How should Black handle this threat to the queen?} Qxh2+ {Retreating the queen would be strategically awful:} (27... Qe7 $2 28. Ne2 {And White is better with f4 - f5 plan on the kingside. Black's dark-squared bishop is offside. I did not want to enter this line, thus the main dynamical resource to change the character of the position.}) 28. Kxh2 bxc3 {And suddenly the c3 -pawn cannot be stopped! Black will regain the material by force.} 29. Qd3 {My opponent found the only resource in this position and offered great resistance:} c2 {Forced, otherwise Qc2 would block the passer.} 30. Qxa6 c1=Q 31. Qxe6+ Kh8 32. Rxc1 Bxc1 {Despite White's extra 3 pawns for the bishop, I managed to coordinate my pieces and won by a mating attack against the white king.} 33. f5 Rc2+ 34. Kh1 Rfc8 {See the relevant Passed Pawn Theme.} *

