1... e4 {Oops, is White in trouble after this pawn fork?} 2. Nd4 {Great defense! Exploiting the drawback of the last move which weakened the d4 -square. The follow-up is also very important.} exd3 (2... Ne5 3. Be2 {And White saves the bishop and obtains a better game due to the strong knight on d4 and the weakness on c6 .}) 3. Nxc6 {And the queen is trapped on d8 ! A very cute short sequence that saves a piece for White! (See the relevant Defensive Theme. )} *

