{Can you spot a strong idea for Black that is based on a very short variation?} 28... Bc4 {Hitting the loose pieces along the d-file and preparing the next move.} (28... Bxf3 $2 {would be a terrible mistake:} 29. Bxf3 Rxd3 30. Rxb7 Rxa3 31. Bd5) 29. Nf2 (29. Nb2 Ba6) 29... Ba6 {Beautiful! Now the a7 -rook is trapped and Black wins. Simple and strong! (See the relevant Positional Theme. )} *

