{A student playing with the black pieces against me.} 35... Be5 {Such a strong multi-purpose move! White has no e4 - e5 anymore, and the bishop is getting ready for the next move with tempo on the rook.} (35... Re7 $4 {Black has to be very careful against White's main idea here:} 36. e5+ $1 Bxe5 (36... fxe5 37. Ne4#) (36... Kxe5 37. Rxe7) 37. Ne4#) 36. Rc2 {The rook has no way in stopping Black's next move. White is losing material.} (36. Rd3+ Kxc5) 36... Bd4+ {Winning the knight on c5 .} *

