22... exd6 {My student resigned against me with White in this position. Can you do better?} 23. Rd1 {An astonishing defense! Preparing the next move.} Nxa1 24. Nd2 {And White is winning a minor piece. Black will have only an extra exchange now, but White will collect the second pawn soon.} Bc6 25. Rxa1 {White is 'only' down an exchange and has a much better pawn structure and an extra pawn. The h3 -pawn is loose. White is very close to equality, which looked impossible from the initial position!} *

