{Lasker - Tarrasch, 1914.} 43. Bf6 {Forcefully creating a passed pawn on the kingside!} gxf6 {In the actual game, this bishop was not captured, however, Black thus lost the g7 -pawn, giving White a very strong passer on h5 .} (43... Ke6 44. Bxg7 {Lasker converted his advantage from here.}) 44. h6 {And the pawn cannot be stopped! Such a lovely idea that is based on a very short calculation!} *

